{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaSrQQexqFTvwvuEYwyk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I proved `length_myRev` in `Main.lean`, and `lean Main.lean` runs with no errors or warnings.\n\n```lean\ntheorem length_myRev (xs : List α) : (myRev xs).length = xs.length := by\n  induction xs with\n  | nil => rfl\n  | cons x xs ih => simp [myRev, ih]\n```\n\nThe proof uses induction on the list:\n- **Empty list:** `myRev []` is `[]`, so both lengths are 0 and `rfl` closes the goal.\n- **Non-empty list (`x :: xs`):** `simp` expands `myRev` to `myRev xs ++ [x]`. It then uses the rule that the length of a joined list is the sum of the two lengths, plus the induction hypothesis `ih`, to reduce the goal to `xs.length + 1 = xs.length + 1`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":448,"cache_read_input_tokens":7851,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":448},"output_tokens":284,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a03a0efa-512d-4abb-9862-f6bd430c6344","uuid":"cce601b2-3110-46c9-ac96-0c30ac932550","timestamp":"2026-10-31T14:08:32.510Z","request_id":"req_011CgaSrQ8HYgAPkwYLc5sey"}
